{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794463301,"nonce":"1w0hy/mjwFp1h8vxwG+Rhw4uudI=","title":"x","message":"Without BuildKit's process sandbox, a RUN process can outlive its RUN and might rewrite /workspace/.scarab-build/oci before the push Step reads it. The content is the author's either way, so this is not a credential issue. But outputs.\u003cid\u003e.image (BuildKit metadata) and outputs.\u003cid\u003e.push.digest can then differ.\nFix: the push Step compares the layout's manifest digest with the build Step's containerimage.digest and fails on a mismatch. Docs already tell deployers to use outputs.\u003cid\u003e.push.digest. Related: dfa1b5f. Found by the Fable review of #182.","files":null}]}